{"id":"000W4Z","title":"Parkour Portal Pathway (ft. Todd)","author":"72kchunshuai","solvedCount":5,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-24T12:40:05+00:00","posted":"Heute, 05:00 Uhr","rules":"I'm very honored to collaborate with Todd, the inventor of Parkour line. He is an incredibly creative setter and a very nice guy to chat with, so I highly recommend checking out his puzzles.\nFor this puzzle we basically followed the ideas of RAT RUN 7: Multiple Choice. The difficulty is around 3* according to testers. Hope you have fun!\n\nRules:\n\n• Normal Sudoku rules apply: Place the digits 1–9 once each in every row, column, and 3x3 box.\n\n• Aim: You are a parkour runner. Reach the drink by finding a path from your spot through the maze. The path passes through the centres of cells. It must not visit any cell more than once, cross itself, or pass through any thick maze walls. You may move orthogonally, and diagonally through an open 2×2 space, but never diagonally through a round wall-spot on the corner of a cell.\n\n• Teleports: A teleport is a coloured oval marked with a letter. Entering one carries you to the other cell with the same letter, and the path continues from there. Cells with the same letter contain the same digit. Cells with different letters contain different digits.\n\n• Black Kropki: A black dot between two cells means one digit is double the other. Not every such pair is marked.\n\n• Parkour line: Digits are building heights. From one cell of the path to the next, the height may change only by +1, +0, −1 or −2.\n\nPlay on SudokuPad\n\n(If the emojis don't display correctly in your browser, please kindly refer to the image above.)","solutionCode":"Digits NOT on the path in column 3, from top to bottom, ??? digits in total.","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/awvy7ub5uh","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/awvy7ub5uh","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","